// =============================================================================
//  probe_save.hml — W4-12's acceptance harness.   BUILD_PLAN W4-12.
// =============================================================================
//
//      hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_save.hml -o /tmp/probe_save
//      /tmp/probe_save                     # compiled — the shipping path
//      hemlock  tools/probe_save.hml       # interpreted — parity
//      nm /tmp/probe_save | grep -c SDL_   # MUST be 0
//
//  Exits 1 on any failed assertion, and asserts its own assertion COUNT so a
//  section that silently stops running is a failure rather than a green run.
//
//  WHAT IT IS ACTUALLY TRYING TO CATCH
//  -----------------------------------
//  A save format has exactly two ways to be wrong, and both of them look fine:
//
//    1. It round-trips the HASH but not the STATE.  `sim_hash` quantizes
//       positions to 1/16 m, so a codec that stored a float as a fixed-point
//       i32 would pass a hash comparison and desync three seconds later.  So
//       this probe compares RAW f64 BIT PATTERNS as well as the hash, and it
//       plants a position whose low mantissa bits do not survive quantization
//       so that the check has something to fail on.
//
//    2. It round-trips the state but not the WORLD the state lives in.  The
//       chunk store is not in `sim_hash` at all.  A load that restored every
//       entity and forgot which chunks were resident would pass every hash
//       assertion at tick 0 and then run on missing terrain.  So this probe
//       does not stop at the round trip: it STEPS BOTH WORLDS FORWARD and
//       compares them every tick.
//
//  It also plants deliberately malformed files — bad magic, a future version,
//  a truncated tail, one flipped byte — and requires a NAMED refusal for each,
//  because "rejected cleanly rather than crashing" is an acceptance criterion
//  and an uncaught exception satisfies neither half of it.
// =============================================================================

